rts there are going to be. Also, I wonder if it's possible for a regular Scion to develop an Epicenter the way it's possible for a Titanic Scion to develop an Innate Ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it wouldn't surprise me if Demigods at minimum develop one, considering they already have Collateral rules, Catastrophic Successes, etc. It would fit right in with the theme of uncontrolled power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T13:04:42-07:00","id":1460249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1457251-saints-monsters-preview?p=1460151#post1460151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I was asking about regular scions getting access to epicenters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Should be pretty easy to house rule given that we already have the model &quot;10 xp to have both epicenter and the innate power&quot;.to apply for appropriate PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T18:17:58-07:00","id":1460280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1457251-saints-monsters-preview?p=1460149#post1460149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh - with how much the more recent material has lead into the idea that the difference between Gods and Titans is political, I\u2019m surprised there would be significant mechanics difference like this (obviously there are the Titan Callings, but while those are more common with Titans, appropriate Gods and their Scions have them too)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Given how Fate works, I'm not that surprised. Politics <i>is </i>reality, when it comes to the divine. Which the Orishas will happily point out, and also why the Atua are confused why there's a diff in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T10:07:13-07:00","id":1484428,"title":"","content":"One of the books I'm reading is &quot;Southern Cunning: Folkloric Witchcraft in the American South&quot; by Aaron Oberon. It's not a how too book, but rather a testimonial of his experiences transforming the stories in &quot;The Silver Bullet and Other American Witch Stories&quot; by Hubert J. Davies. It seems to correspond to the patronage category of Sorcerer as he sought initiation by the Witch Father. Note that there are different Witch Fathers for different areas. There is also a price paid in sickness and job loss. He also mentions that afterwards he was presented with hundreds of situations where Witchcraft was necessary to find a solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}